  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Salient Crgt obligated $824M in FY2026 to date across 53 awards, with an average award size of $15.5M and year-over-year change up 0.9%. Salient Crgt’s FY2026 obligations are slightly above FY25 obligations of $816M and continue a multi-year increase from $240M in FY21, $405M in FY22, $505M in FY23, and $557M in FY24. Salient Crgt’s work is highly concentrated in a single NAICS: Computer Systems Design Services, which accounts for $735M of FY2026 obligations. Salient Crgt receives most federal spending through one agency. The General Services Administration obligated $545M to Salient Crgt in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $136M and the Department of Homeland Security at $52.3M. Other purchasers include the Department of Defense at $46.3M and several smaller agencies. The mix of obligations shows a services-heavy profile focused on computer systems design and engineering services, with limited obligations in training, language schools, and selected R&D categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Salient Crgt's agency customers?",
        "body": "Salient Crgt’s agency revenue is highly concentrated. The General Services Administration obligated $545M, which represents the single largest buyer. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Homeland Security are the next largest buyers at $136M and $52.3M respectively. Remaining agencies each account for materially smaller obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What industries capture most of Salient Crgt's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services dominates Salient Crgt’s portfolio with $735M in FY2026 obligations. Engineering Services is the second-largest market at $61.6M, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $17.8M. Other listed NAICS categories show only modest or zero obligations."
      }
    ]
