  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Salient Crgt make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Salient Crgt obligated $824M from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Salient Crgt received that total across 53 awards with an average award size of $15.5M and year-over-year change up 0.9%. FY2026 obligations are slightly higher than FY25 obligations of $816M and continue the increase from prior years, including $557M in FY24 and $505M in FY23."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Salient Crgt?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Homeland Security are the leading buyers from Salient Crgt. The General Services Administration obligated $545M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $136M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $52.3M in FY2026 to date. Other buyers include the Department of Defense at $46.3M and several smaller agencies such as the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation at $16.8M and the Commodity Futures Trading Commission at $13.6M."
    },
